<title>UK: Inchcape buys Peru drink brands.</title>
<headline>Inchcape buys Peru drink brands.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>British diversified group Inchcape Plc said on Monday its Peruvian unit Embotelladora Latinoamericana SA (ELSA) had bought the San Luis table water and Kola Inglesa carbonated soft drink brands.</p>
<p>Inchcape said the transaction valued the brands and assets at $39.1 million.</p>
<p>Inchcape said San Luis was the largest table water brand in Peru and the combination with ELSA's San Antonio brand would give Inchcape a dominant position in the mineral water market.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
